l, impact query or responder routing is in the repo. | Run the E12 drill: mark helpdesk-mcp compromised, query affected instances, quarantine, revoke, alert. | [] | []\nR01 gap agent_team | Tool error bodies from the gateway or helpdesk-mcp reach the model as free text with no schema, size, injection or redaction checks. | Replace exc.detail in src/agent.py:188 with a fixed message (keep detail only in the redacted audit), and stop forwarding upstream.text in src/gateway.py:184. | [('src/agent.py', 188, \"Tool error text goes into the model context with no validation. exc.detail is the upstream error body (gateway passes upstream.text[:2000], src/gateway.py:184; on the direct route it is helpdesk-mcp's own body or JSON-RPC error message, src/gateway_client.py:91-94). Success payloads go through validate_tool_output; error bodies skip schema, content screening and redaction.\")] | ['R01.1', 'R01.2', 'R01.4']\nR02 gap security | Tool results are labelled by source and trust, except error results, which pass raw upstream text unlabelled; containment otherwise rests on code-level approval gates. | Wrap error results in the same source/trust envelope with fixed text; add repeated and adaptive injection tests with success rates. | [('src/agent.py', 71, 'Outside content never enters the system prompt.')] | ['R02.2', 'R02.5']\nR03 gap agent_team | Tool error text reaches the model unredacted, although success output, logs and audit rows are redacted. | Send only a fixed error message to the model; confirm the HR portal blocks remote images (CSP img-src). | [('src/agent.py', 188, 'Error text is redacted for the log line (src/agent.py:187) but passed to the model unredacted; tool output (src/validation.py:74), chunks and audit records are redacted.')] | ['R03.1', 'R03.2']\nR04 gap agent_team | The handbook search cache is keyed without the employee id, so employee-specific documents cached for one employee are returned to another. | Include employee_id (and audience set) in PolicyIndex._key, or cache only audience='all' rows; add a test with two employees issuing the same query. | [('migrations/001_init.sql', 102, 'Only the ingest role can write chunks.')] | ['R04.3', 'R04.4']\nR07 gap agent_team | Context tokens are stored only on model_call rows; action rows carry none, missing cache counts become 0, and approved actions run under a new trace. | Write context_tokens and method on every action row and keep the trace link across approval resume. | [('src/agent.py', 79, 'Context size is recorded per model decision step.')] | ['R07.1', 'R07.2', 'R07.4']\nR08 needs_evidence security | Denials are recorded, but no security detection rules or alert routing are in the repo. | Provide SIEM rules over audit.events/gateway_decisions and their routing to a named responder; run recipe R08. | [] | ['R08.1', 'R08.2', 'R08.3']\nR09 needs_evidence security | Each consequential action is checked by the employee against a rendered description, but sequence and context-range detection is not in the repo. | Provide sequence rules and per-context-range results (recipe R09). | [('src/approvals.py', 31, 'The employee checks each consequential action without the untrusted content.')] | ['R09.1', 'R09.2', 'R09.3']\nR10 needs_evidence security | No second-model reviewer or misalignment scope statement is in the repo. | Record whether deliberate misalignment is in scope; if so run recipe R10, otherwise seek N/A approval. | [] | []\nR11 gap operations | An agent_type stop is enforced only inside the agent; the gateway's stop query omits that scope, and a gateway error routes escalations around the gateway. | Add agent_type (from a verified claim, not the header) to the gateway stop query; remove the direct_route fallback; run a dated drill (recipe R11). | [('src/gateway.py', 99, \"The agent loop checks all five scopes before each model call (src/killswitch.py:17-26), but the gateway's stop query covers fleet, agent_instance, subject and agent_principal only. A stop set on scope agent_type is enforced only by the agent's own code; the gateway still forwards that agent type's tool calls. When the gateway's stop query fails it returns 503 and escalate_to_human goes straight to helpdesk-mcp (src/gateway_client.py:51-59).\")] | ['R11.1']\nR12 gap agent_team | No per-operation stop policy exists, and a timed-out write is handed back to the model as an ordinary error instead of a tracked hold. | State stop behaviour per tool in config/tools.yaml; on unknown outcome, place a hold with an owner and block retries until reconciled with HRIS/helpdesk. | [('config/tools.yaml', 55, 'No code or config states, per operation, whether file_leave_request or create_ticket can be cancelled, completed or only reconciled after a stop.')] | ['R12.1', 'R12.3']\nR13 gap agent_team | Most steps are audited, but a GatewayUnavailable for non-direct tools escapes without a step record, and SDK retries and direct-route fallbacks are not recorded. | Catch GatewayUnavailable in _execute and audit it; record retries, fallbacks and operation ids. | [('src/agent.py', 193, 'Each step writes a linked record.')] | ['R13.1', 'R13.4']\nR14 gap agent_team | A 503 from the gateway, which can follow a forwarded call, triggers an automatic resend of the helpdesk ticket on the direct route without reconciliation. | Remove the direct_route resend; on 503 after send, mark the outcome unknown and reconcile with helpdesk-mcp by Idempotency-Key. | [('src/gateway_client.py', 86, \"Any 503 from the gateway is treated as 'not delivered' and escalate_to_human is resent on the direct route. The gateway returns 503 for any exception, including after it has already forwarded the call upstream (for example a failed audit write at src/gateway.py:190 or a bad upstream JSON body at :185). The result is unclear, yet the client resends instead of pausing for reconciliation.\")] | ['R14.1', 'R14.2', 'R14.3', 'R14.4', 'R14.5']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011vTFYNkqUKYpBci5aZir9o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
